      "writtenOn": "2021-02-03T22:30:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Icelake is a misnomer at this point, there were changes made to support dedede \u0026 volteer instead of splitting off jasperlake and tigerlake PS modules.\n\nCorrect. In my opinion, we should have just split the power sequencing for TGL and JSL into their own separate units as well.\n\n\u003e I wonder what the downside of creating a per-baseboard power sequencing module isn\u0027t maybe more effective, even if it involves copy and paste? \n\n+1. It adds a little more copy-paste, but I think organization wise it can be much cleaner.\n\n\u003e Were there two different chromebook programs using the same Intel CPU that were able to share a PS module without at least some hooks for customization?\n\nI think this goes back to the time where we did not support baseboard model in ec, and instead copied stuff across multiple boards for the same platform (e.g. SKL). Maybe we need to re-evaluate this and use baseboard as the location for power sequencing logic. We do see differences in power sequencing design across programs using the same SoC as well e.g. Hatch v/s Puff. Puff went with a separate sequencing unit and I think that was a good decision.",
      "parentUuid": "29fbe4a7_9f308990",
      "revId": "cddbf692f268d2cb851590567f4a7ef678f8e9fc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2f3e040f_ea32e530",
