      "writtenOn": "2021-02-03T22:33:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I think this goes back to the time where we did not support baseboard model in ec, and instead copied stuff across multiple boards for the same platform (e.g. SKL). Maybe we need to re-evaluate this and use baseboard as the location for power sequencing logic. We do see differences in power sequencing design across programs using the same SoC as well e.g. Hatch v/s Puff. Puff went with a separate sequencing unit and I think that was a good decision.\n\nExactly. History makes sense too. My vote is for brya to just have its own power sequencing module, based on icelake, using intel_x86 where needed",
      "parentUuid": "cf557773_d54acf0a",
      "revId": "cddbf692f268d2cb851590567f4a7ef678f8e9fc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
