      "writtenOn": "2021-02-04T07:59:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "just keep in mind that none of these power sequencing\nchanges are due to alderlake.\nintel\u0027s adlrvp[mp]_ite use the existing power/icelake.c.\nbrya has a custom power sequencer chip, hence the customizations.\n\nif we were to clone and tweak icelake.c, it would be for brya,\nnot alderlake. the only question in my mind is whether this would\nbe a baseboard or board level customization. if partners decide\nto not follow the reference board style power sequencing, this\nwould be demoted to a board level feature. i\u0027m tending toward\nbaseboard rather than board.\n\ni can give this a try to see how the restructuring ripples through.",
      "parentUuid": "2f3e040f_ea32e530",
